[{:db/id "q-115680/selection/63fb4a94312eeb96bccbccd12a3e3176654c247549cec8ac7790fa90572dcd93" :answer/id #uuid "6ebf00d3-3445-578b-8668-59f876e606bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115680/selection/78cac38c81af6ccb5378e1d88651f678e3c09c456a378f1e90638ba37cc0fbf2" :answer/id #uuid "886a0ce8-3f20-59a1-9a36-8b939388b11e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=3x(x+2)(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115680/selection/ec0ad90298247b3d35f39d9dac870d4c0dc9fc3ad4da0cf041cda8e4c5d577f3" :answer/id #uuid "cca2a13a-ad44-530b-942d-c12dd1df933c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=2(x-2)(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115680/selection/8d774de593d9922e87fcf68e6a805b9d09b801f0cfa3ea1708f176e9ae73a12a" :answer/id #uuid "c1d030f5-1f64-5b10-b9f5-9006f93918da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115680/selection/3baf6c7581c2e977a438d56b0a4858c73036f1720b41c5bca4feebae86ce5069" :answer/id #uuid "d20a6edc-0b56-5519-a58a-f0283047aacb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115680/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57b45219-5e5b-5375-b470-70dca3deab45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115680/selection/63fb4a94312eeb96bccbccd12a3e3176654c247549cec8ac7790fa90572dcd93" :answer-field/choices ["q-115680/selection/63fb4a94312eeb96bccbccd12a3e3176654c247549cec8ac7790fa90572dcd93" "q-115680/selection/78cac38c81af6ccb5378e1d88651f678e3c09c456a378f1e90638ba37cc0fbf2" "q-115680/selection/ec0ad90298247b3d35f39d9dac870d4c0dc9fc3ad4da0cf041cda8e4c5d577f3" "q-115680/selection/8d774de593d9922e87fcf68e6a805b9d09b801f0cfa3ea1708f176e9ae73a12a" "q-115680/selection/3baf6c7581c2e977a438d56b0a4858c73036f1720b41c5bca4feebae86ce5069"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115680" :question/id #uuid "692cfb5d-4022-59e1-9118-b329cfd0c2b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115680" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/ac782575d30a0f87e5a930ae03ef91f9c606cc03baa5b4ff9037f871a63fccd9.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f2ad5a7c6ea5a224583246a32e0da6de66c834f4d87be1b5bc646d3c7a678163.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-2$ and $x=4.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should equal zero on both of these lines.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x) \\\\ {y}^{′} & =(x+2)(x-4)^{2} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =3x(x+2)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can dismiss the equation ${y}^{′}=3x(x+2)(x-4)^{2}.$ Although the right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ it also evaluates to zero when $x=0,$ which is behavior not exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-2$ and $x=4$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-2$ | $-2<x<4$ | $x>4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}(4-x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115680/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5277f56d-3f2d-505c-bf73-48207a2310a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115680"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "eefcb27e-5e07-5e48-8515-f487bdba4b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "7c388f6d-06c3-56ed-894c-413649f71971" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "65edacab-7ff2-5a88-a7a0-94eee027bde4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "8ab39b6f-f235-5b4c-8f1e-b1228a89c75f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0d8ab2fa-5a90-5ba3-a296-416e05865e03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5adaf710-fbe4-5980-adc6-dbbee2f20e9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115754/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-115754/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-115754/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-115754/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-115754/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-115754/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115754" :question/id #uuid "b507f238-cfcf-5089-bfe0-5c0eb3e8d978" :question/math-academy-id "q-115754" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/34af8d1078100aea331c300ea529d2fdefbdd31e99ee8a7946325d58a8abf680.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=7-{x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/d02883b776dbcd55c5c96347ed1a7bb0e51ef8c26e62786049b6585b878d04fb.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-7.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=7-{x}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not approach $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -7.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(1+\\frac{7}{x})}\\to -\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{x+7}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115754/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32b9a92b-880b-50de-b8e9-648fa219b83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854/selection/5d85aa5005033441bdefd9ef1865cd15097ec2488025f3a00b62f7cd4edac9a1" :answer/id #uuid "ffb4c567-db8d-5e15-80f9-6c4bf25aace3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854/selection/a64d8493b6ea2fe09828e7215abe90cc7ce4d8f33c7e25158a24c7469f1b71ac" :answer/id #uuid "930f182c-6108-54dc-a387-0fe85d5341d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854/selection/1b894375ebc91ddeb45f1c503cee6347bed44657602255cb5f123c2b4e590d74" :answer/id #uuid "685a799e-0458-5fc0-b9f7-507e356bfdda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854/selection/61fb999d16ff4a47b8a522f88978980051f8915924cfa3245e0cd7813321879a" :answer/id #uuid "165edf21-9ad5-5fa5-9dc5-f2bcdf27e7e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=\\frac{x-4}{x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854/selection/a937cdd5bbd419cd22a7f0b0967becb164b863292b7a06fde355a314fa1b47d8" :answer/id #uuid "a770575a-f9e0-5ee8-884b-ff606def3fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c49507a2-8e68-5e3c-8b2d-bea589b06489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115854/selection/a937cdd5bbd419cd22a7f0b0967becb164b863292b7a06fde355a314fa1b47d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-115854/selection/5d85aa5005033441bdefd9ef1865cd15097ec2488025f3a00b62f7cd4edac9a1" "q-115854/selection/a64d8493b6ea2fe09828e7215abe90cc7ce4d8f33c7e25158a24c7469f1b71ac" "q-115854/selection/1b894375ebc91ddeb45f1c503cee6347bed44657602255cb5f123c2b4e590d74" "q-115854/selection/61fb999d16ff4a47b8a522f88978980051f8915924cfa3245e0cd7813321879a" "q-115854/selection/a937cdd5bbd419cd22a7f0b0967becb164b863292b7a06fde355a314fa1b47d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115854" :question/id #uuid "89e18e48-808b-5b06-800c-06851f8a0fc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115854" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/753554f8129ab0ed83f19e5cadefba27cb3b700818bd3a3f801c64aaf01ded70.png)\n\nIdentify the differential equation that generated the slope field above." :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f26e5b61c573664f0397667aff82cfe5d918e0d22f005658862c28c53d5de748.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the solution curves have vertical asymptotes $x=2$ and $x=4.$\n\nOf the given equations, the only two that satisfy this condition are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}=\\frac{1}{(x-2)(x-4)}\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{(x-2)(x-4)}.\n$$\n\n- Second, the slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$ \n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(1-\\frac{6}{x}+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ do *not* become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115854/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32b9a92b-880b-50de-b8e9-648fa219b83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115854"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "57e36753-df3a-52be-96a7-9ed7dc740a62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "39f88868-529c-56e6-9e64-ca215ecae98f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "61ff83c6-07d2-55c3-887a-9fb68aae42f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "5a06c7d0-902f-5339-a59b-8c312a7dba04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2d950ea1-d226-5a39-9862-ebcd24979c70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86552279-0187-5297-8acf-504f348f3aa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120038/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-120038/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-120038/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-120038/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-120038/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-120038/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120038" :question/id #uuid "cdeb6520-9bfc-52b8-b6bf-9364334ae71a" :question/math-academy-id "q-120038" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f855062048a7d38b2fa6c843701a182661b2235b2042ad83fbedd600b1dd770c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/8fdec9bda9e2bcc514e56a14a6608b2f0cb74fd0943a51c944b29cc047e02cd9.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$ gives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=2,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5277f56d-3f2d-505c-bf73-48207a2310a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073/selection/b95fde67f32fd4e96023c0e3974a5a7fe9c74cb64b931ee382267a996e31a763" :answer/id #uuid "b1fdb470-663e-5475-a85a-fdd51dce8ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073/selection/e58cace463da641b5e5b9a8d8ee8feb33dae89003ffca08128f8f740244364a8" :answer/id #uuid "eb0b0a13-be25-595f-a3ba-6f115430d206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}={x}^{3}+2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073/selection/8b795881aaf7433cc75ca3b9686d1f959b2564e393b9744c9b95a8000526f074" :answer/id #uuid "2c0cf95d-b9ea-526d-8701-e33b1bbe54d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073/selection/be304bb9650ad3783cad1325c7cb42d02b030ee872ee0af0df8981271e7bcac7" :answer/id #uuid "3f8b431d-c4e7-5d28-9d97-bafe62db64df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073/selection/4f0c965c42b58249554f193f308b21880f602d5e5857da38a4e5515ec648c759" :answer/id #uuid "83db9486-e3f2-5358-b3d4-4014dee5d515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{′}=2x-{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f4437bc-1d30-51cb-b923-4ebea8e02482" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120073/selection/b95fde67f32fd4e96023c0e3974a5a7fe9c74cb64b931ee382267a996e31a763" :answer-field/choices ["q-120073/selection/b95fde67f32fd4e96023c0e3974a5a7fe9c74cb64b931ee382267a996e31a763" "q-120073/selection/e58cace463da641b5e5b9a8d8ee8feb33dae89003ffca08128f8f740244364a8" "q-120073/selection/8b795881aaf7433cc75ca3b9686d1f959b2564e393b9744c9b95a8000526f074" "q-120073/selection/be304bb9650ad3783cad1325c7cb42d02b030ee872ee0af0df8981271e7bcac7" "q-120073/selection/4f0c965c42b58249554f193f308b21880f602d5e5857da38a4e5515ec648c759"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120073" :question/id #uuid "5bc105c8-71b1-5687-8bc1-c61b80acb528" :question/math-academy-id "q-120073" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/1135d4a7b28f5cd1ab046f89e2882cd9074b43f95b2076b261e04003e4330c14.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069297/assets/f68f830dd6d0e6fb205bfa1ac56b1818b676089a12a5bcab46699210ba9e3191.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on these lines.\n\nOf the given equations, the only two that satisfy this condition are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x=x(x+2)(x-2),\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}={x}^{2}(2+x)(2-x).\n$$\n\n- Second, the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2$ divide the plane into $4$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-2$ | $-2<x<0$ | $0<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↘$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x=x(x+2)(x-2).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}={x}^{3}-4x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120073/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "762c5225-00bd-5d2f-9859-394f886482cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120073"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
